Roast.pet Frontier Stack =E2=80=94 2 useful finds 1) Pruna P-Video-2-Pro =
=E2=80=94 TEST NOW

Release: September 17, 2026. Newly discovered in this scan; not released
this hour.
Source:
https://docs.pruna.ai/en/stable/docs_pruna_endpoints/performance_models/p-v=
ideo-2-pro.html

What changed: Pruna has shipped a MiniMax H3-derived production video
endpoint with explicit Speed and Quality recipes, first-frame plus optional
last-frame conditioning, generated audio, 5=E2=80=9315 second clips, 480p/7=
68p
output and seed control. The unusually important part for Roast.pet is
economics/latency: 480p Speed is $0.02/sec and 768p Speed $0.035/sec;
Quality is $0.04/$0.075 per second respectively. Pruna currently documents
50% promotional pricing through September 24. Runware documentation reports
the model as released Sep 17.

Capability: cheap canonical-pet I2V drafts and first/last-frame constrained
AR loops. Inputs: prompt + optional first/last frame +
duration/resolution/mode/seed. Output: 24fps video with generated audio.
API: Pruna Predictions API; also distributed through Runware/Replicate and
other hosts. Privacy: cloud-hosted, so pass canonical PetAsset rather than
raw customer uploads. Commercial/license: production API is available, but
this scan did not find a sufficiently explicit standalone model-weight
commercial license; treat this as hosted-API use and verify provider ToS
before production. Constraint: it does not accept an uploaded audio track,
so it cannot directly replace deterministic TTS + lip-sync.

Exact Roast.pet use: use Speed mode to create 3=E2=80=935 cheap motion cand=
idates
from the approved podium card, QC/rank them, and only invoke Quality/H3
Max/Wan/LongCat when the draft fails. First+last-frame conditioning is also
a direct test for seamless QR/AR loops.

Smallest test: 20 canonical pets =C3=97 5-second 480p Speed ($0.10 nominal =
each
at current documented rate), then compare usable-generation rate and pet
identity against H3 Max Turbo. Repeat winners at 768p Speed/Quality.
Measure wall-clock latency, identity drift, fur/marking retention and
actual billed cost.

Decision: TEST NOW.
2) BytePlus LAS AI 1.5.3 =E2=80=94 Storyboard Script Generation + Intellige=
nt Video
Remix =E2=80=94 WATCH/TEST

Release: September 18, 2026.
Source: https://docs.byteplus.com/en/docs/Byteplus_LAS/las_release_notes

What changed: LAS added a Storyboard Script Generation operator that
converts scripts plus character/prop/scene asset JSON into a standardized
storyboard_bundle, plus Intelligent Video Remix that uses ASR, semantic
retrieval and model orchestration to automatically match, sort and edit
voice-over/B-roll/source footage into a final video.

Capability relevant to Roast.pet: it could replace custom glue for turning
roast JSON + PetAsset + selected voice + generated clips into deterministic
multi-shot social variants. Inputs: script/natural language, asset JSON and
media; outputs: storyboard bundle / assembled video. Route: BytePlus LAS
managed operators. Pricing/license: not established reliably in this scan;
managed cloud service. Privacy: cloud processing, therefore avoid raw
customer photos after canonicalization. Constraint: likely overkill for a
simple 5=E2=80=9315 second roast, and deterministic FFmpeg/Remotion may rem=
ain
cheaper and more controllable.

Exact use: feed roast script, canonical pet asset and generated reaction
clips into the storyboard/remix layer to create 9:16 TikTok/Reels variants
automatically.

Smallest test: one 3-beat roast with fixed assets; compare operator output
against the current deterministic finisher for timing, captions,
reproducibility, latency and total cost.

Decision: WATCH/TEST, not core-stack adoption yet.
TOP 5 STACK CHANGES TO TEST NOW

   1. P-Video-2-Pro Speed as the ultra-cheap draft renderer before premium
   escalation.
   2. LongCat vs H3 Max Lip Sync vs Wan 2.7 specifically on real cats/dogs.
   3. Local pet cutout =E2=86=92 automated QC =E2=86=92 Knockout fallback.
   4. Multi-take TTS =E2=86=92 comedy ranking before paying for animation.
   5. Unified audiovisual QC =E2=86=92 automatic retry / premium-render esc=
alation.

CHEAPEST meaningful capability improvement: P-Video-2-Pro 480p Speed is
documented at $0.02/output-second, making a 5-second candidate about $0.10
at the current published rate. This is cheap enough to generate multiple
candidates rather than betting on one render.

BIGGEST CAPABILITY SHOCK THIS HOUR: not a new foundation model, but
H3-class audiovisual generation becoming cheap/fast enough that best-of-N
rendering is economically plausible for a low-ticket personalized Etsy
product.

CONCRETE STACK SIMPLIFICATION: formalize VideoRenderer.generate(PetAsset,
RoastSpec, tier) and use P-Video-2-Pro Speed for draft, then automated QC;
only route failures or premium orders to H3/Wan/LongCat. Keep deterministic
customer-selected TTS/lip-sync as a separate route because P-Video-2-Pro
cannot ingest audio.

Scanner note: searches across GitHub, Hugging Face, fal/Replicate, WebXR,
segmentation, TTS, Etsy/POD and workflow releases produced no other item
that cleared both novelty and Roast.pet relevance thresholds;
mature/unchanged tools were suppressed.

